## Goal
Record the user's acceptance of ADR 0006 (DEV-49, "Ask when no rule matches a link from an app") by moving its status to accepted.

## Problems
None. The user's acceptance was only needed before merge, so development was not blocked.

## Decision
The user confirmed the ADR after a summary of the behavior. The commit only changes the status in `docs/adr/0006-ask-unmatched.md`. The ADR describes:
- A panel appears when a link from an app matches no rule. "Keep default" (Dia · Private) comes first, then the profiles from the user's rules.
- The "Remember" checkbox appends a host rule at the end of the rules file, so it never overrides existing rules.
- If the default profile is chosen, the rule is written as `open: {default: true}`, so the host follows any later change of default profile.
- The feature can be turned off with a settings checkbox or with `ask_unmatched: false` in the rules file.

The known consequence is that every unmatched app link will prompt after install, and prompts get rarer as rules are remembered.

